Z||000000||fieroX||12-05-2001||03:56 AM||||I havent gotten anywhere near this point of the swap yet, but I am always thinking ahead about how im going to do something.  I was wondering what it takes to make the stock guages work with the L67 since there are different frequencies in todays electronics that wasnt available back in good ol 87.  I figured maybe the VSS was the same, but a friend of mine told me the coil pack ignition is way different than what the 2.8 has.  So what all does it take to make them work?<P>------------------<BR>   coming soon L67 powered 87 coupe<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fierox.com/logo2small.gif">     <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroX.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroX.com</A> <p>[This message has been edited by fieroX (edited 12-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||12-05-2001||06:43 AM||||Depends on the PCM you're using. My VSS had to be changed to the newer style but the speedo is computer driven at the stock Fiero 4000 pulses/mile and the tach is also computer driven so no changes nessary. Not sure on the oil pressure sender. Those are the only 3 things that could present a problem.||||reg||1
